<title>ITALY: Alitalia restarts flights to Ethiopia.</title>
<headline>Alitalia restarts flights to Ethiopia.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alitalia said it will restart flights from Rome to the Ethiopian capital, Addis Ababa on June 3 following a five year break, an Alitalia spokesman said.</p>
<p>The service was discontinued on March 31,1992.</p>
<p>The new twice weekly flights will operate Tuesday and Friday and use a Boeing 767 with a 22 tonne cargo capacity, the spokesman added --Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
